  {
    "unit_id": "U02",
    "rule": "The word for the changes with the noun: il before a masculine noun (il libro, il dottore), la before a feminine one (la casa, la donna), and l' before any noun that starts with a vowel (l'uomo). Lui is he and lei is she. È, with its accent, means is; e without one means and. Questo and questa mean this: questo with a masculine noun, questa with a feminine one. An adjective in -o changes to -a with a feminine noun (piccolo, piccola); one in -e stays the same (grande, forte).",
