    "unit_id": "U06",
    "rule": "For more than one, a masculine noun in -o changes to -i (libro, libri) and a feminine noun in -a changes to -e (mela, mele). A few are irregular: uomo becomes uomini. The word for the changes too: i for most masculine plurals (i libri), gli before a vowel (gli uomini, gli amici), le for feminine plurals (le mele). Noi siamo is we are, voi siete is you are when speaking to several people, and loro sono is they are; abbiamo, avete and hanno are the same three forms of avere.",
