    "rule": "Some feelings use essere with an adjective, which agrees with the person: a man says Sono stanco, a woman Sono stanca; malato and malata work the same way, while felice and triste don't change. Others use avere with a noun, where English says to be: Ho fame is I'm hungry, Ho sete I'm thirsty, Ho sonno I'm sleepy, Ho paura I'm afraid, Ho freddo I'm cold and Ho caldo I'm hot.",
