    "rule": "To describe someone, Italian uses avere with the: Ha i capelli lunghi, she has long hair; Ho gli occhi azzurri, I have blue eyes. The adjective comes after the noun and agrees with it, so plural capelli and occhi take lunghi and azzurri. Alto describes a man and alta a woman. A piedi means on foot.",
