    "unit_id": "U41",
    "rule": "To ask a friend's name, say Come ti chiami? To ask politely, to someone you don't know, say Come si chiama? That is Lei, the polite you: it is the same word as lei (she) and takes the same verb form, so si chiama means both her name is and your name is. Answer with Mi chiamo … (my name is …). Piacere! means pleased to meet you, and Ti presento … (Le presento …, politely) introduces someone.",
